Z||000000||Cooter||03-13-2000||09:56 PM||||I took these pictures to show the difference between the 2.8 and 3.4 exhaust manifolds.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroport_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/portrestrictions.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/34port.jpg"> <BR>The top picture is the exhaust port of the Fiero manifold that measures 1.5 inches.<BR>The middle picture show the restrictions in the ports that everyone needs to remove to improve flow.<BR>The bottom picture shows the outlet of the 3.4 manifold that measures 1.75 inches. The Y pipe for the 3.4 measures 2.25 inches where the manifolds join it and connect to the converter.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||03-14-2000||09:49 AM||||What vehicle did the 3.4 manifolds come off, Camaro? Are the manifolds approximately the same length as the 2.8 manifolds, just bigger outlets?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||03-14-2000||04:15 PM||||They are Camaro manifolds. The entire manifold is different looking. It is really better looking than the Fiero pieces- smoother looking passages and should be more durable because it is cast iron. If I can ever get all my stuff together for the engine swap, I will post pic's of the exhaust system.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-14-2000||05:35 PM||||According to one source, they put those 3.4 engines in Camaros from 93-95 and I found Pace Setter headers that will fit this application. Probably would not work in a Fiero engine compartment, but I'm tempted to order a pair to find out for sure. If they can't be made to fit, then send them back. I called all the local boneyards and they don't have the factory 3.4 exhaust manifolds.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||1
